# v18 verification log — annotation-scope fix, difficulty_cte_folded rename, standardized subset comparison
# Date: 2026-09-02 (UTC)

## Changes in v18 (relative to v17, external review follow-up)

Mandatory wording corrections:
1. Author contributions: the co-author's 100 independently designed queries are
   now described as "主評価245クエリに含まれる100クエリの独立設計" (a subset of
   the 245-query main evaluation), not an additional validation set.
2. Data availability and S10 step 3: both 100-query sets are explicitly
   labelled "（主評価245クエリの部分集合）".
3. §2.1.2: the manuscript no longer claims that all 245 main queries carry
   explicit required-table / JOIN-path annotations. It now states that every
   query has a gold SQL and expected result (JSON); required tables and JOIN
   structure are derived from the gold SQL for the multi-axis comparison
   (sec:multiaxis); explicit required-table/JOIN-path annotations are kept
   separately only for the 100-query ablation subset. Verified against the
   package: main_evaluation_dataset.jsonl 245 rows have no
   expected_tables/required_tables/required_join_path/expected_columns fields;
   evaluation_dataset.jsonl (ablation 100) has expected_tables 100/100 and
   required_join_path 100/100.

Catalog rename:
4. build_query_catalog.py: column `difficulty_unified` renamed to
   `difficulty_cte_folded` (design-time label with CTE queries folded to
   very_hard). This is unrelated to the post-hoc structural-complexity proxy of
   compute_unified_difficulty.py (144/245 agreement with historical labels);
   the rename removes that ambiguity. query_catalog.csv / query_catalog.json
   regenerated (300 rows; regeneration is byte-identical / deterministic).
   `grep -rn difficulty_unified` over the staging tree (excluding
   verification_logs/, whose logs mention the old name when describing this
   rename): 0 hits.

Supplement wording:
5. 「統一複雑さスコア」→「設計時難易度層のpost-hoc複雑さ指標」 in the
   supplement; §2.1.2 and the untranslated-EN-25 paragraph use the same
   framing.
6. significance_recomputed.json `_meta.test`: "exact distribution" →
   "SciPy method='exact' distribution" (regenerated; content identical except
   generated_at, timestamp restored).

Exploratory standardized comparison (recomputed from existing saved outputs
only; no paid LLM calls):
7. compute_all_figures.py now derives, from the single saved main run
   (main_eval_with_sql.json), per-difficulty recall for the independent-design
   subset (100) and the author-designed complement (145), and a direct
   standardization of both to the main-corpus difficulty mix (E43/M69/H69/VH64)
   using unrounded stratum means:
     independent standardized  83.9 %
     author-designed           89.4 %   (difference 5.5 pp; VH stratum is the
                                         only reversal: 85.7 vs 74.8)
   Stored in paper_data.json under
   independent_evaluation.main_run_subsets.{by_difficulty,
   standardized_to_main_distribution}; manuscript §4.3.1 reports it as an
   exploratory observation (not a causal self-reference-bias estimate).

README notes:
8. README_SQL.md documents that q_expert_101–115 keep historical ID naming but
   are NOT part of the independent 100 (author-designed), and that
   semantic_contract exists only on q_expert_014 / q_expert_038 (metadata
   granularity, not a separate dataset).

PDF:
9. \usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}: link boxes removed from the Japanese PDF.

